# .agent/env.example — the tokens this project's agent container needs.
#
# This file is DOCUMENTATION (committed). Real values never live here — put them
# in the two env files below (both gitignored / outside the repo). `agent init`
# never writes secrets anywhere.
#
# ── Project tokens → ./.env (repo root, gitignored) ──────────────────
# GH_TOKEN is required for every launch: the container clones and pushes over
# HTTPS with it (no SSH keys ever enter the container). Mint a fine-grained PAT
# scoped to THIS repo at https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta with:
#   • Contents      Read and write   (clone, commit, push)
#   • Pull requests Read and write   (open/update PRs)
#   • Issues        Read and write   (file follow-up issues)
#   • Actions       Read             (inspect CI status)
#   • Metadata      Read             (mandatory baseline)
# Then, in ./.env:
#   GH_TOKEN=github_pat_...
# Add any deploy tokens and every key listed in config.js `requiredEnv` here too.
#
# ── Agent credentials → ~/.config/agentic-coding/env (host, all projects) ──
# Shared across every project on this machine:
#   CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=...   # from `claude setup-token` on the host
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=...            # optional; codex prefers a host `codex login`
